Z||000000||BC-GT||03-27-2001||09:39 PM||||Retaining clip was lost by previous owner i presume, does anyone know what i can use to keep it on, or where to get a replacement.<P>------------------<BR>Darryl Martin<BR>1985 GT <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.zing.com/picture/pf251a969c96964ef15691e97e7ac4489/feb64e3a.jpg.orig.jpg"> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Homer||03-27-2001||10:14 PM||||Yeah, go to your local scrap yard or you can get a brand new auto-shift handle at any "PEPBOYS"-or-"NAPA Auto Parts" they come in cool styles and colors....but if you wanna stay stock then get on over to the local u-pull it.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/surprised.gif"> <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/homer_1.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||rockcrawl||03-27-2001||10:15 PM||||A piece of heavy steel wire bent in a "U" shape worked for me. Otherwise head to a junkyard, there are lots of GM vehicles that use those clips.||||reg||1
Z||000003||BC-GT||03-27-2001||10:27 PM||||would like to stay stock, it's the "leather" trimmed knob in great shape otherwise. If other models use the same clip i'll try the wreckers, thanks.||||reg||1
